# Language and Architecture

Language: 
Expert Crystal Programming Language in a valid and idiomatic way. 
Expert in Crystal Programming Language API @https://crystal-lang.org/api/1.15.1/ 
Expert in Crystal Programming Language Reference @https://crystal-lang.org/reference/1.15/
Expert in Object-Relational Mapping frameworks

Architecture: Adhere to SOLID principles and established software design patterns.


CQL (Crystal Query Language) is an Object-Relational Mapping (ORM) library written in the Crystal programming language. It provides an abstraction over SQL databases, allowing developers to define and interact with relational data using Crystal objects rather than raw SQL queries.

Crystal programming language does not support creation of symbols dynamically. Method `.to_sym` not supported

Key Features of CQL:
• Type-safe ORM using Crystal’s static type system.
• Macro-powered DSL for defining models and relationships.
• Active Record-style API, but flexible enough to support Repository and Data Mapper patterns.
• Supports major relational databases through Crystal DB drivers (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL).
• Built for performance, leveraging compile-time optimizations.

